            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "not a major risk, but this AI flag seems legitimate 😭 \r\n\r\n>  The minimal swap restores only curwin/curbuf — not globaldir/tp_localdir, which the prior full-restbuf path did restore. In the auc_win branch, aucmd_prepbuf sets `globaldir = NULL` and `curtab->tp_localdir = NULL` (autocmd.c:1413-1418). So a redraw during an autocmd operating on a hidden buffer could now evaluate directory-dependent statusline content with the wrong cwd:\r\n  - `%f/%F` when the real window's path is relative to a `:lcd`\r\n  - `%{getcwd()} / %{expand('%:~:.')}` in a custom statusline\r\n",
            "commit_id": "c84024de8bb7c38d884a1b1a909d615bdf8e4c15",
            "created_at": "2026-06-24T13:25:55Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -466,8 +466,11 @@ int update_screen(void)\n   }\n \n   // Restore actual curwin before redrawing.\n-  if (autocmd_save.save_aucmd != NULL && curwin->handle != autocmd_save.save_curwin_handle) {\n-    aucmd_restbuf(&autocmd_save);\n+  win_T *save_curwin = autocmd_save_curwin ? win_find_by_handle(autocmd_save_curwin) : NULL;\n+  win_T *restore_curwin = save_curwin != NULL ? curwin : NULL;\n+  if (save_curwin != NULL) {\n+    curwin = save_curwin;\n+    curbuf = curwin->w_buffer;",
